@startuml status-menu-bar
' cumin works - the monitor file and the menu bar app: cumin run writes the file, the app and cumin status only read it.
' Document: status-menu-bar.md, topic on the two parts and the contract.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

actor Maintainer
actor Operator
cloud "GitHub" as github

rectangle "cumin run (Go)" as run
file "monitor.json\n&#126;/.local/state/cumin/" as status
file "status-bar.json\n&#126;/.config/cumin/" as config
rectangle "menu bar app (Swift)\ntools/status-bar/" as app
rectangle "macOS menu bar" as bar
rectangle "cumin status (Go)" as statuscmd

run -left-> github : poll
run --> status : write a temporary file,\nthen rename:\nafter every poll,\nat the end of a run
app -up-> status : read every 5 s
statuscmd -up-> status : read at every call:\nlast poll, its errors,\nagents
Operator -up-> statuscmd : run
app -left-> config : read every 5 s
app --> bar : three segments (glyph and count),\nlist with links, old file,\nsound and blink
Maintainer -up-> bar : look, open a link
Operator -up-> config : edit

note bottom of status
  The only contract between the two parts.
  cumin run is the only writer.
  cumin run never reads the file.
  cumin status reads it for its report only.
  No token, key, webhook address,
  or usage number.
end note

note bottom of app
  No network call, no Keychain read,
  no third-party dependency.
end note
@enduml
